<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  WildAnimals_Greentide.xml                 UtinniPatches — new file 2026-09-22
  ============================================================================

  Puts the campaign's Greentide fauna roster onto RM_Greentide, replacing the
  deliberate Core-only roster that src/RimMandrake/Greentide/Defs/BiomeDefs/
  RM_Greentide_Biome.xml ships (Warg, Muffalo, Elephant, Cobra, Megaspider,
  Rat, Hare — kept there so the Greentide mod is self-contained and works with
  nothing else loaded). The campaign wiring lives HERE, never in the Greentide
  mod itself.

  WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST. §7 Q11 (owner, 2026-09-22): "RimMandrake should
  not name star wars ever." So RM_Greentide may not carry this cast, and at
  Phase B of design/RimMandrake/biome_mod_architecture.md the RUT_Greentide def
  that currently carries it dies and RM_Greentide takes the tiles. Without this
  patch in place by then, the Greentide would lose its entire cast on the live
  world. WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml is the shape this copies.

  🔑 SOURCE OF TRUTH (AT AUTHORING, 2026-09-22): every weight below started as
  a verbatim copy of Defs/BiomeDefs/RUT_Greentide.xml's own wildAnimals block
  (frozen 2026-09-22, the roster the world runs on today). Nothing was
  rescaled at that time. 🔴 This is NO LONGER a byte-for-byte mirror — see the
  RSW_CanopySwinger row below (COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1, 2026-09-25): new
  campaign fauna for the Greentide is added HERE from now on, never to the
  frozen RUT_Greentide.xml, so this file and that one WILL diverge going
  forward and that is correct, not drift to reconcile.

  🔴 ONE ROW WAS DROPPED FROM BOTH, DELIBERATELY: the dianoga. Owner ruling
  2026-09-23, verbatim: "It's a mistake to have dianoga in the GreenTime. It
  belongs only in tank prisons and the Fever Wood. Create something new and
  terrifying for the Green Tide."

  ⇒ MEASURED after that removal and before the addition below: this file and
  RUT_Greentide.xml each carried 26 rows summing to 9.168. This file now
  carries 27 (RSW_CanopySwinger fills the vacated slot) summing to 9.468;
  RUT_Greentide.xml stays at 26/9.168 by design (frozen). Any doc still
  quoting 26/26 parity, or 27 rows / 9.318 from before the dianoga ruling, is
  stale. ⛔ Do not
  "restore parity" by adding the dianoga back to either file.

  ✅ An earlier owner review had already ordered it out of the Greentide
  (rosters/the_greentide.json: disposition "move:AB_MiasmicMangrove"); the move
  was never executed in the defs, and the row survived here only because this
  file copied the roster verbatim. The vacated slot is reserved for a NEW
  creature — never a neighbour's species.

  🔴 OUR DEFS, NOT THE DONOR'S. Owner ruling 2026-09-19, verbatim: "They should
  be using OUR creatures, not the donor references. The donor references, if
  any, should never be used again." RUT_Greentide still names 21 rows as
  mlie.starwarsanimalcollection's bare defNames (Gizka, Convor, Nuna...) —
  MEASURED 2026-09-23, down from 22 because the dianoga row is gone. All
  21 exist as our own RSW_ ports — MEASURED 2026-09-22, each confirmed present
  as BOTH a PawnKindDef and a ThingDef, which matters because a wildAnimals key
  resolves to a PawnKindDef and a ThingDef name there fails silently. This file
  casts the ports:

    Gizka        -> RSW_Gizka         Clodhopper   -> RSW_Clodhopper
    Whisperbird  -> RSW_Whisperbird   Worrt        -> RSW_Worrt
    Shiro        -> RSW_Shiro         ShiroTrap    -> RSW_ShiroTrap
    Klorslug     -> RSW_Klorslug      Mott         -> RSW_Mott
    Nuna         -> RSW_Nuna          Convor       -> RSW_Convor
    Falumpaset   -> RSW_Falumpaset    Gelagrub     -> RSW_Gelagrub
    Kinrath      -> RSW_Kinrath       Fambaa       -> RSW_Fambaa
    PekoPeko     -> RSW_PekoPeko      Dalgo        -> RSW_Dalgo
    Hawkbat      -> RSW_Hawkbat       Hssiss       -> RSW_Hssiss
    Dragonsnake  -> RSW_Dragonsnake   Lylek        -> RSW_Lylek
    Beldon       -> RSW_Beldon

  RSW_Diggerpede was already ours in the source def. The two AA_ rows and the
  one VFEI2_ row are non-Star-Wars donors, so §7 Q9 would allow them inline on
  RM_Greentide — but that mod's own header commits it to a Core-only roster
  ("no third-party or franchise-specific fauna, no MayRequire on a third-party
  bestiary"), so they are cast here too and RM_Greentide stays pure Core.

  ============================================================================
  DELIBERATELY NOT IN THIS FILE YET — see SW_FAUNA_NEVER_IN_RM_TIER_1
  ============================================================================

  1. THE 8 STAR WARS wildPlants. RUT_Greentide's plant list carries
     Plant_HydenockTree_Wild 1.5, Plant_JoganTree_Wild 1.2, Plant_MujaFruit_Wild
     1.0, Plant_HubbaGourd_Wild 0.8, Plant_FelucianGlowspore_Wild 0.6,
     Plant_Bubblespore_Wild 0.5, Plant_Chakroot_Wild 0.5, Plant_TookeTrap_Wild
     0.5 — all mlie.starwarsanimalcollection. MEASURED 2026-09-22: only TWO have
     our ports (RSW_Plant_HubbaGourd_Wild, RSW_Plant_Chakroot_Wild); the other
     SIX do not exist as ours. Casting the donor names is forbidden by the
     2026-09-19 ruling above, and casting only two would leave the campaign
     Greentide nearly flowerless at Phase B — so the whole plant block waits on
     DONOR_DEFS_PORT_TO_OURS_1 porting those six. ⛔ Do not "fix" this by
     reaching for the donor defNames. STILL PENDING as of the
     SW_FAUNA_NEVER_IN_RM_TIER_1 audit, 2026-09-25 — this is a real dependency,
     not an oversight.

     🔴 `RUT_YearningFruit` is NOT one of the 8 above and is not blocked by
     that dependency — it is a wholly new plant authored for this campaign
     (GREENTIDE_YEARNING_FRUIT_1, COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1), defined in
     UtinniPatches itself
     (Defs/ThingDefs_Plants/RUT_YearningFruit.xml), so it is always loaded
     whenever this file is — no MayRequire needed, same posture as the
     RUT_Sytheclaw wildAnimals row above. Wired below.

  🔴 REVISED 2026-09-26 (GREENTIDE_EXOTIC_JUNGLE_FISH_1) — the 2026-09-25
  fishTypes fix below was WRONG in one respect: it added the whole
  `<maxFishPopulation>` + `<fishTypes>` block unconditionally, which made
  RM_Greentide's fish catch depend on RUT_ items that only exist when
  UtinniPatches (the campaign) is loaded — the exact "thin dependency-free
  fallback" shape §7 Q11a forbids for an RM_ mod, just on the fish axis
  instead of the fauna axis this whole file otherwise exists to prevent.
  RM_Greentide_Biome.xml now ships its own franchise-free
  `maxFishPopulation`/`fishTypes` inline (RM_Zeev/Uvva/Karrun/Dubbol/Lozh/
  Saava/Tuun/LungerFry, new RM_-tier duplicates of the RUT_ table — never
  the RUT_ defNames themselves), so Op 5 below now does only what this
  file's other SW ops already do: ADD the two canon scalefish catches
  (RSW_FaaCatch/RSW_LaaCatch) and the common one (RSW_MeeCatch) onto the
  now-existing freshwater buckets, gated on mandrake.rsw.swbestiary same as
  every other row here. rareCatchesSetMaker is untouched by this file —
  RM_RareGreentideCatches (the base file's own def) already carries an
  RSW_LaaCatch bonus option gated on its own `<li>`, so no patch op is
  needed for the rare table either.

  ⚠️ RUT_Sytheclaw is cast under its current live defName. §7 Q10 renames it to
  RM_Sytheclaw as part of its own seven-creature sweep; this file follows that
  rename when it happens, it does not front-run it. Note also that the sytheclaw
  is wired to BOTH the Greentide (0.2 here) and the Pyrelands (0.2, in
  WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml), which BIOME_SPECIFIC_FAUNA_LAW_1 has yet to
  adjudicate — that is one of its 52 multi-homed species, not a defect of this
  file.

  ============================================================================
  STRUCTURE AND VERIFICATION
  ============================================================================

  Shorthand-dictionary form throughout (`<RSW_Gizka>1.0</RSW_Gizka>`) — the only
  form BiomeAnimalRecord.LoadDataFromXmlCustom reads, same as the Pyrelands file.
  Op 1 REPLACES the node (dropping the Core-only roster) with the one def this
  mod itself always ships; ops 2-4 then Add onto the now-existing node behind the
  gate for each cast's home mod. Every op is wrapped in a
  PatchOperationConditional on the target node, so the whole file is a silent
  no-op if mandrake.rm.greentide is ever not loaded.

  ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing logs nothing — PatchOperationConditional
  returns true on no match, and an unmatched PatchOperationAdd is silent. A clean
  validate_patch.py run is NOT proof a row landed. 🔴 UNVERIFIED AGAINST A LOAD:
  authored on the Mac laptop, where there is no def dump and no game
  (GREENTIDE_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 step 5 is owed). Confirm all 26 rows from a
  post-load def dump on the Desktop before believing this file works — and
  confirm the dianoga is ABSENT, which is the 2026-09-23 ruling's live test.
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- Drop RM_Greentide's Core-only roster and seat this mod's own def. Guarded
       on the target node rather than on a donor: RUT_Sytheclaw ships with
       UtinniPatches itself (Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RUT_PyrelandsPortedFauna.xml),
       so it is always loaded whenever this file is. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Greentide"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Greentide"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <wildAnimals>
          <RUT_Sytheclaw>0.2</RUT_Sytheclaw>
        </wildAnimals>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- The Star Wars cast, all 22 as OUR OWN RSW_ defs (never the donor's bare
       names — owner 2026-09-19). Weights verbatim from RUT_Greentide.xml.
       (22, not 23: the dianoga row was removed 2026-09-23, see header.) -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Greentide"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Greentide"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <RSW_Gizka>1.0</RSW_Gizka>
        <RSW_Clodhopper>0.7</RSW_Clodhopper>
        <RSW_Whisperbird>0.7</RSW_Whisperbird>
        <RSW_Worrt>0.7</RSW_Worrt>
        <RSW_Shiro>0.5</RSW_Shiro>
        <RSW_ShiroTrap>0.5</RSW_ShiroTrap>
        <RSW_Diggerpede>0.4</RSW_Diggerpede>
        <RSW_Klorslug>0.4</RSW_Klorslug>
        <RSW_Mott>0.4</RSW_Mott>
        <RSW_Nuna>0.4</RSW_Nuna>
        <RSW_Convor>0.3</RSW_Convor>
        <RSW_Falumpaset>0.3</RSW_Falumpaset>
        <RSW_Gelagrub>0.3</RSW_Gelagrub>
        <RSW_Kinrath>0.3</RSW_Kinrath>
        <RSW_Fambaa>0.25</RSW_Fambaa>
        <RSW_PekoPeko>0.2</RSW_PekoPeko>
        <RSW_Dalgo>0.18</RSW_Dalgo>
        <RSW_Hawkbat>0.18</RSW_Hawkbat>
        <RSW_Hssiss>0.18</RSW_Hssiss>
        <!-- RSW_Dianoga 0.15 REMOVED 2026-09-23 — owner ruling, see the header.
             ⛔ Do not restore it. The slot is reserved for a new creature. -->
        <!-- RSW_CanopySwinger fills that reserved slot — COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1
             (2026-09-25), ledger slug the_greentide:canopy-swinger, the_greentide.md
             §4's "the Swingers" — a genuinely NEW creature (reuses RSW_KowakianMonkeyLizard's
             body/art asset only, not the species itself; see RSW_CanopySwinger.xml's own
             header), never a neighbour's. This is the first row ADDED beyond this file's
             original verbatim mirror of RUT_Greentide.xml (that file is FROZEN, do not edit —
             see its own banner — so new campaign fauna for the Greentide is wired HERE from
             now on, not there). RUT_Greentide.xml itself does not carry this row and must
             not: the live world still runs on that frozen def until Phase B's repaint, and
             this row only reaches players once RM_Greentide takes the tiles. -->
        <RSW_CanopySwinger>0.3</RSW_CanopySwinger>
        <RSW_Dragonsnake>0.12</RSW_Dragonsnake>
        <RSW_Lylek>0.05</RSW_Lylek>
        <RSW_Beldon>0.008</RSW_Beldon>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Alpha Animals: the floor-vermin needlepost and the margin-predator blood
       shrimp. Non-Star-Wars donors, so Q9 would permit these inline on
       RM_Greentide — cast here instead to keep that mod's Core-only promise. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Greentide"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Greentide"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <AA_Needlepost>0.3</AA_Needlepost>
        <AA_BloodShrimp>0.2</AA_BloodShrimp>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- VFE Insectoids 2: the swarmlings. Same reasoning as the Alpha Animals
       block above. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="oskarpotocki.vfe.insectoid2">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Greentide"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Greentide"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <VFEI2_Swarmling>0.4</VFEI2_Swarmling>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- GREENTIDE_YEARNING_FRUIT_1, 2026-09-26. RUT_YearningFruit onto
       RM_Greentide's wildPlants — commonality 1.2, matching the weight the
       roster's own annotation gave this exact "the fruit yearns to be
       eaten" design line (rosters/the_greentide.json, attached there to
       Plant_JoganTree_Wild before this item split the mechanic into its own
       new plant). No MayRequire: this def ships with UtinniPatches itself,
       same reasoning as the RUT_Sytheclaw wildAnimals op above. Guarded on
       the target node existing, same PatchOperationConditional shape as
       every other op in this file. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Greentide"]/wildPlants</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Greentide"]/wildPlants</xpath>
      <value>
        <RUT_YearningFruit>1.2</RUT_YearningFruit>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- GREENTIDE_EXOTIC_JUNGLE_FISH_1, 2026-09-26 (revises the 2026-09-25
       SW_FAUNA_NEVER_IN_RM_TIER_1 op — see the header note above for why).
       RM_Greentide_Biome.xml now ships fishTypes/maxFishPopulation inline
       with its own franchise-free RM_ catch defs, so this file only ADDS the
       three canon scalefish catches onto the buckets that already exist —
       same MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary" gate every other SW row in
       this file uses, no dependency on RUT_ or on UtinniPatches itself. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Greentide"]/fishTypes/freshwater_Common</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Greentide"]/fishTypes/freshwater_Common</xpath>
      <value>
        <RSW_MeeCatch>0.4</RSW_MeeCatch>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Greentide"]/fishTypes/freshwater_Uncommon</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Greentide"]/fishTypes/freshwater_Uncommon</xpath>
      <value>
        <RSW_FaaCatch>0.3</RSW_FaaCatch>
        <RSW_LaaCatch>0.3</RSW_LaaCatch>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
